{"name":"Jacaranda Jazz","hex":"#6c70a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jacaranda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several trees, of the genus Jacaranda, native to tropical South America, that have pale purple, funnel-shaped flowers. In horticultural use refers specifically to Jacaranda mimosifolia.","The hard, dark wood of these trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacaranda"},{"term":"jazz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical art form rooted in West African cultural and musical expression and in the African American blues tradition, with diverse influences over time, commonly characterized by blue notes, syncopation, swing, call and response, polyrhythms and improvisation.","Energy, excitement, excitability."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To destroy; to ruin.","To play (jazz music)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jazz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jacaranda","blocks":[{"text":"Jacaranda is a genus of 49 species of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae, native to tropical and subtropical regions of the Americas and cultivated around the world. The generic name is also used as the common name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Jacaranda_cuspidifolia_flower.jpg/330px-Jacaranda_cuspidifolia_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacaranda","wikidata":"Q311105"},{"title":"Jazz","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz is a music genre that originated in the African-American communities of New Orleans, Louisiana, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Its roots are in blues, ragtime, European harmony, African rhythmic rituals, spirituals, hymns, marches, vaudeville song, and dance music. Since the 1920s Jazz Age, it has been recognized as a major form of musical expression in both traditional and popular music. Jazz is characterized by swing and blue notes, complex chords, call and response vocals, polyrhythms and improvisation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz","wikidata":"Q8341"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Jacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Jacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Jacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Jacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jacaranda leaves in Elifelet Garden, Tel Aviv","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Jacaranda_seedling.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Jacaranda_seedling.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Jacaranda seedling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacaranda_seedling.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg/250px-Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg/330px-Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg/250px-Jacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacaranda_ulei_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jacaranda_seeds.jpg/250px-Jacaranda_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe